meta {
  name: Get Curated Patient Data
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/v1/patients/:patientId/curated-patient-data/:classificationGroupType
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:path {
  patientId: {{patientId}}
  classificationGroupType: vaccinations
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  Returns curated patient data for one classification group. The response schema is selected by `classificationGroupType` and identified by the matching discriminator in the response body. Partner-facing display text is returned without literal `|` separators, while identifiers, patient keys, URLs, source metadata, codes, statuses, dates, timestamps, and contact fields are preserved as received.

  ### Availability

  Curated Data availability depends on your Predoc contract. Use this endpoint when structured clinical data is included in your workflow; otherwise, use the document endpoints to retrieve patient records in their original formats. Contact your account manager if you are unsure which endpoints are enabled for your organization.

  ### Fields

  | Field | Description |
  |---|---|
  | `patientId` | Unique identifier of the patient. |
  | `classificationGroupType` | Curated patient data classification group to retrieve. |

  ### Example response 200 OK

  ```json
  {
    "classificationGroupType": "allergies",
    "partnerPatientId": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
    "patientKey": "patient-key-123",
    "items": [
      {
        "patientId": "11111111-1111-4111-8111-111111111111",
        "allergyId": "allergy-1",
        "practitionerRoleId": "practitioner-role-1",
        "allergyCodes": [
          "91935009"
        ],
        "name": "Peanuts",
        "recordedDate": "2024-01-20",
        "onsetStartDate": "2024-01-15",
        "onsetEndDate": null,
        "reactionManifestation": "anaphylaxis",
        "reactionManifestationCodes": [
          "39579001"
        ],
        "sources": [
          {
            "source": "HIE",
            "retrievalDate": "2026-04-01"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  }
  ```
}
